          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Pierre\",\"addressee\":\"Hélène\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Je vous aime!\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.98,\"reason\":\"The focal expression directly presents Pierre's love for Hélène as true. Its hesitant, formulaic delivery may bear on sincerity or depth of feeling, but it does not remove the clear avowal force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"да и я люблю ее\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime!\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"reason\":\"The words themselves do not undertake marriage, fidelity, future conduct, or another obligation. The scene already identifies Hélène as Pierre's fiancée before he speaks, so the surrounding engagement must not be transferred onto this separate love avowal. No undertaking by Pierre is established through the focal expression itself, and no distinct uptake of such an undertaking occurs.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Пьер молча держал руку своей невесты\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Что-то такое особенное говорят в этих случаях\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.96,\"reason\":\"The utterance is not represented as an involuntary or reflex-like discharge of affect. Pierre deliberately recalls the socially expected words and then says them; embarrassment about their poor effect does not make them an expressive outburst.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"сказал он, вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"слова эти прозвучали так бедно, что ему стало стыдно за себя\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":1,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.76,\"reason\":\"Beyond avowing love, the expression weakly functions as performance of an expected romantic social formula. The narration explicitly frames it as what one was supposed to say in such circumstances, though this residual scripted function remains secondary to the avowal.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"слова эти прозвучали так бедно\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"After Pierre and Hélène have already been treated by those present as engaged and are left alone, Hélène kisses Pierre. He thinks that it is now too late and that he loves her, then utters the focal French declaration because he remembers that such words are expected on this kind of occasion. The narration emphasizes its awkward and impoverished sound.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"mixed\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The focal expression contains no explicit undertaking. The surrounding scene has already socially established Hélène as Pierre's fiancée, but the supplied evidence does not make “Je vous aime” itself a new promise or proposal. Hélène gives no separately represented verbal uptake to this avowal after it is spoken. Evidence of affection is mixed: Pierre internally thinks that he loves her, while the scene also depicts pressure, hesitation, shame, and formulaic delivery.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"The supplied passage is recognisable as Leo Tolstoy's War and Peace. The classification relies only on the supplied text.\",\"limitations\":\"The evidence supports analysis of the utterance's represented force and immediate circumstances, but it does not conclusively settle the depth or sincerity of Pierre's love. No omitted context is treated as absent from the work.\"}"
        }
